      "text": "#1 [Hint]\nThe maximum area is when the circle is perfectly inscribed in the square. Use $2r=s\\sqrt{2}$ to find the radius $r$.\n#2 [Solved by RichxD3] The area of the circle is much smaller than that of the square because a circle is a universal shape. Find a big circle. Then, draw the square from the center of the circle to the sides, then subtract it from the area of the circle.\n#3 [Solved by RichxD3] The circle has radius of 2.5 inches. This means that the side of the square is 5 inches. The area of the circle is $pi \\left(2.5\\right)^2$, and the area of the square is $5\\times5$.  They differ by $0.995...$ square inches.",
