      "text": "To determine by how many square inches the area of the circle is greater than the area of the square, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Find the side length of the square using the diagonal given.\n2. Calculate the area of the square.\n3. Find the radius of the circle using the diameter given.\n4. Calculate the area of the circle.\n5. Determine the difference between the areas of the circle and the square.\n\nLet's solve this step by step using Python:\n\nFirst, we find the side length of the square from the diagonal.\n\\[ \\text{side length} = \\frac{\\text{diagonal}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\]\n\nThen, we calculate the area of the square:\n\\[ \\text{area\\_square} = \\text{side length}^2 \\]\n\nNext, we find the radius of the circle:\n\\[ \\text{radius} = \\frac{\\text{diameter}}{2} \\]\n\nThen, we calculate the area of the circle:\n\\[ \\text{area\\_circle} = \\pi \\times \\text{radius}^2 \\]\n\nFinally, we find the difference between the areas:\n\\[ \\text{difference} = \\text{area\\_circle} - \\text{area\\_square} \\]\n\nWe can use Python to perform these calculations accurately.\n```python\nimport math\r\n\r\n# Given values\r\ndiagonal_square = 5\r\ndiameter_circle = 5\r\n\r\n# Calculate side length of the square\r\nside_length_square = diagonal_square / math.sqrt(2)\r\n\r\n# Calculate area of the square\r\narea_square = side_length_square ** 2\r\n\r\n# Calculate radius of the circle\r\nradius_circle = diameter_circle / 2\r\n\r\n# Calculate area of the circle\r\narea_circle = math.pi * (radius_circle ** 2)\r\n\r\n# Calculate difference in areas\r\ndifference = area_circle - area_square\r\n\r\n# Round the difference to the nearest tenth\r\ndifference_rounded = round(difference, 1)\r\nprint(difference_rounded)\n```\n```output\n2.4\n```\nThe area of the circle is greater than the area of the square by \\(\\boxed{2.4}\\) square inches.",
